<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine bolsa's MerVal drops five stocks.</title>
<headline>Argentine bolsa's MerVal drops five stocks.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's weighted MerVal stock index dropped five stocks in its quarterly revision based trading volume, the Argentine bolsa said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The stocks shed were power utility Capex, agricultural holding company Cresud, cement maker Juan Minetti, sugar refiner Ledesma and oil company Sol Petroleo.</p>
<p>Effective Thursday, when trading resumes after a two-day New Year break, the MerVal roster will be as follows:  </p>
<p>Acindar</p>
<p>Alpargatas</p>
<p>Astra</p>
<p>Banco Frances</p>
<p>Banco de Galicia</p>
<p>Banco del Sud</p>
<p>Celulosa</p>
<p>Central Costanera</p>
<p>Central Puerto</p>
<p>Ciadea</p>
<p>Comercial del Plata Indupa</p>
<p>Ipako</p>
<p>Irsa</p>
<p>Molinos Ro de la Plata</p>
<p>Telecom</p>
<p>Telefnica</p>
<p>Transportadora de Gas del Sur.</p>
<p>Perez Companc</p>
<p>Polledo</p>
<p>Sevel</p>
<p>Siderar</p>
<p>Siderca</p>
<p>YPF</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom 541 318-0657))</p>
</text>
